From ec5a1e1dfdae7d5ffeb95e46508719fa13a9b5c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: colum <colum@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 11:00:31 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] drafter: TF_DS_LORA applies a PEFT adapter to the DSpark
 blocks' attention projections as an additive epilogue (y += (alpha/r) * B *
 (A * x)) on the rank's own slice, off by default

The drafter fine-tune could not be served without re-quantizing and splicing the 196 GiB pack. This
adds a runtime adapter: TF_DS_LORA=<dir> loads one PEFT folder (adapter_config.json and
adapter_model.safetensors) at load and validates it against the plan - the rank, the alpha, the
target modules and each tensor's dtype and unsharded shape - so a bad folder, or a missing directory
with the switch on, fails the model open rather than the first request. TP2: a rank uploads only its
own slice by the same plan its weights came from (plan.Split, the DSpark blocks' TP2 split inside the
pair): wq_b's B rows are the rank's heads' output columns, wo_b's A columns are the rank's groups'
input rows, and the replicated wq_a and wkv take the whole adapter. The epilogue is two cuBLAS GEMMs
into a scratch plus the family's add_bf16 kernel, and rope_heads for wq_b (whose output the glinear
already roped), issued on the engine's stream inside Drafter.body, so PassGraphs' capture records it
and a replay keeps it; no EXL3 trellis kernel changes. wo_a's grouped slices and the experts are not
targeted.

With the switch unset, or a zero adapter (rank 0, an empty target list, alpha 0), nothing is
allocated and no launch is issued: the pass is bit-identical to base, and a module the adapter does
not target is a no-op. Multiple adapters, hot reload, per-class acceptance tuning and quantized
adapter storage are deferred.

Tests: zig build test passes, including the new host tests in lora.zig: the switch's off states, the
config's rank/alpha/target rules (PEFT's rslora and DoRA refused), the shard's tiling (rank 0 and
rank 1's wq_b B rows and wo_b A columns disjoint and complete, the replicated projections whole), a
fixture folder's tensors and every mismatch (missing directory, missing model, wrong shape, unknown
target module, a non-bf16 dtype), and the epilogue's arithmetic on a host stub (y += (alpha/r) * B *
(A * x), the rope only on wq_b, nothing for an untargeted module or a zero scale).
